    "narrative": "Today\u2019s optimal lineup for LawDog centers on the favorable matchup against Ritchie, with **Geraldo Perdomo** (72.66) and **Matt Chapman** (70.20) pacing our production. **Geraldo Perdomo** benefits from a strong park factor and a soft xERA of 5.41, maximizing his efficiency score. We are also heavily leaning into the Ritchie matchup for **Luis Arraez** (66.77), **Jung Hoo Lee** (64.90), and **Drew Gilbert** (53.47); while **Drew Gilbert** sits at the bottom of our starters due to his lower-order placement, the 19% SP skill bonus against a subpar arm makes him a viable play to hunt for those elusive stolen bases. **Tyler Freeman** (67.71) remains a high-value anchor, as his promotion to the #2 spot combined with Assad\u2019s 4.52 xERA provides a significant ceiling boost for our Roto categories.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Masyn Winn** (41.39), who fell just shy of the cutoff. Despite his speed profile, **Masyn Winn** is hamstrung today by a difficult encounter with Rodriguez (3.45 xERA), leading the model to prioritize the higher-upside platoon advantages found in **Bryson Stott** (66.64) and **Gavin Sheets** (52.20). While we keep a close eye on the health status of **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Will Smith**, and **Daulton Varsho** on the IL, our current depth remains focused on exploiting these specific SP matchups. Managers should note that **Taylor Ward** carries some inherent risk today against Kirby (3.60 xERA); his score of 45.19 is our lowest start, and he is essentially functioning as a volume play to protect our game caps while keeping our stolen base potential alive.",
